{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c39a6bf8-20de-4ebf-ad0b-b7cb300d0424","step":{"id":"s1","script":"For two fair, independent coin flips, start with the first flip. Heads and tails each have probability one half.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"C1","content":"Two fair coin flips"},{"op":"diagram","id":"tree","region":"left","primitives":[{"kind":"point","at":[0.1,0.5],"label":"Start"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.1,0.5],[0.45,0.28]],"stroke":"solid","label":"H: 1/2"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.1,0.5],[0.45,0.72]],"stroke":"solid","label":"T: 1/2"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c39a6bf8-20de-4ebf-ad0b-b7cb300d0424","step":{"id":"s2","script":"From either first result, the second coin again has two equally likely outcomes. Each complete path records both flips in order.","ops":[{"op":"line","id":"hhbranch","canvas_id":"tree","from":[0.45,0.28],"to":[0.85,0.12],"stroke":"solid","label":"H: 1/2"},{"op":"line","id":"htbranch","canvas_id":"tree","from":[0.45,0.28],"to":[0.85,0.4],"stroke":"solid","label":"T: 1/2"},{"op":"line","id":"thbranch","canvas_id":"tree","from":[0.45,0.72],"to":[0.85,0.6],"stroke":"solid","label":"H: 1/2"},{"op":"line","id":"ttbranch","canvas_id":"tree","from":[0.45,0.72],"to":[0.85,0.88],"stroke":"solid","label":"T: 1/2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c39a6bf8-20de-4ebf-ad0b-b7cb300d0424","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The four outcomes are HH, HT, TH, and TT. Exactly one head occurs on two paths: HT and TH.","ops":[{"op":"point","id":"hh","canvas_id":"tree","at":[0.85,0.12],"label":"HH"},{"op":"point","id":"ht","canvas_id":"tree","at":[0.85,0.4],"label":"HT"},{"op":"point","id":"th","canvas_id":"tree","at":[0.85,0.6],"label":"TH"},{"op":"point","id":"tt","canvas_id":"tree","at":[0.85,0.88],"label":"TT"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Which paths contain exactly one head?","expected_gist":"HT and TH."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c39a6bf8-20de-4ebf-ad0b-b7cb300d0424","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Multiply probabilities along a path: each outcome has probability one quarter. Add the two matching paths, giving one half for exactly one head.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"pathprob","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"P(HT)=P(TH)=\\frac12\\times\\frac12=\\frac14"},{"op":"equation","id":"answer","anchor":{"el":"pathprob","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"P(\\text{exactly one head})=\\frac14+\\frac14=\\boxed{\\frac12}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
